On 13 September 2016 at 13:08, selpahi <seladwa@gmx.de> wrote:

> Nothing new has been approved by the BPFK.


That's disappointing. I had been surprised that the proposal was so
piecemeal and so flagrantly progressive, but of course also pleased that in
fixing some of what is broken, the BPFK would take a broad view of what
counts as brokenness.

(On the matter of online Lojban communities, the List is the only one I
belong to, but surely it is true that the centres of activity must have
moved elsewhere.)

--And.

